Relationship Between TR & MR (When Price remains Constant)
Linear Relationship: In perfect competition, the TR curve is a straight line
with a constant slope, as price remains fixed.
MR is Constant: Marginal Revenue (MR) is constant and equal to the
price, as each additional unit sold contributes the same amount to TR.
TR Increases Proportionally: TR increases by the same amount with each
additional unit sold because the firm is a price taker.
• MR = Slope of TR: The slope of the TR curve represents MR, which is
constant in perfect competition.
(TR at Zero Output: When output is zero, TR is also zero because no units
are sold.
Positive TR Growth: As output increases, TR grows positively without
diminishing returns because MR is constant.
